# Every route is the same document. Without this, opening /shelf directly --
# a bookmark, a shared link, a reload -- is a 404 on a static host, because
# there is no /shelf file to serve. Cloudflare Pages reads this file from
# the build output; the 200 is what makes it a rewrite rather than a
# redirect, so the address bar still says /shelf.
#
# Issue #124: the destination is "/" (a directory), not "/index.html" (a
# file) -- confirmed live, with a three-file marker deployment against the
# real Cloudflare Pages project, that a 200-rewrite naming a file is
# silently ignored and falls through to the platform's own automatic SPA
# fallback instead. This file was never the one actually deployed (the
# assembled artifact's own root _redirects, apps/site/scripts/assemble.mjs,
# is -- and had the exact same bug, fixed there first), but it carried the
# identical broken pattern for whenever apps/web ships standalone.
/*    /   200
